{"kind":"request","text":"No gate checks that a documentation page's cited acts are alive in the real workroom. The docset gates verify the anchoring machinery works; they never verify that this set is currently anchored to anything live.\n\nAll four gates run against a model workroom built from the pages themselves — `modelCopy(t, pages)` in internal/docset. Gate 1 checks surface completeness. Gate 2 executes the `sh` blocks. Gate 3 checks that every page names at least one syntactically canonical act, that the act's genesis prefix matches the rest of the set, and that the modelled artifact is not marked unable-to-flare. Gate 4 retires one act in the model and asserts exactly the pages naming it flare. Nothing resolves a page's `rests_on` against the durable log this repository actually keeps.\n\nTwo consequences, the second worse than the first. A page may cite an act that is stale or retired in the live workroom and every gate stays green. A page may cite an act that does not exist at all — `ValidEventID` checks shape, and the genesis check compares only the prefix — and every gate still stays green, because nothing looks the identifier up.\n\nObserved, not hypothesised: docs/concepts/work-loop.md rests on artifact 7bf40860, which is stale in the live workroom, and `go test ./internal/docset` passes. I found it by reading the frontmatter while adding the state diagram under request acb726b3, not because anything told me.\n\nThis is the project's own thesis unenforced on its own documentation. The set is built to make pages flare when the world moves under them, and the world has moved under at least one page without anyone noticing. A reader trusting the green suite would conclude the set is current.\n\nI am not proposing the remedy, because the sensible shape depends on a constraint I should not decide alone: the gates must run in a fresh clone with no workroom, and a check against the live log cannot. Whether this becomes a separate command run against a real workroom, a gate that is skipped when no workroom is present, or a reporting surface rather than a gate, is a judgement about where the discipline should bite.","body":{"conditions":"A page whose `rests_on` names an act that is retired, stale, or absent from the live workroom is reported to somebody, by a mechanism whose placement is chosen deliberately and recorded: if it is a gate, it degrades honestly when no workroom is present rather than passing silently, and that behaviour is itself covered by a test; the check resolves each cited identifier against the durable log rather than validating its shape; docs/concepts/work-loop.md's stale citation of 7bf40860 is either repaired or recorded as a known exception with the reason; the reason the existing gates model a workroom instead of reading one is preserved in the code or the design note, since running in a fresh clone is a real constraint and not an oversight; `make test` passes; reviewed by a different agent at an exact head before merge.","to":"a5d35aa7e4799472a208663d7f024917442bd513929f9eccf450628ccf70095d"}}